<h1>Curriculum Overview</h1>

<h3><b>What is AI and the Systems that Power It about?</b></h3>

<p>This unit explores how AI and computing systems process information and interact with hardware and software, through hands-on design, troubleshooting, and ethical evaluation of AI's real-world impact.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;">
<p>This is the second unit in the six unit <a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-2026/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: bold;">AI Foundations</a> semester 1 course. This professional learning module prepares you to teach it!</p>
</div>

<h2>Student Learning Goals</h2>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">
<h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Students will:</h3>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Explain how AI and computing systems process information and interact with hardware and software.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Design, troubleshoot, and optimize computing systems while exploring emerging technologies like IoT and robotics.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0;">• Apply human-centered design principles to develop AI-driven solutions for real-world problems.</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy, reliability, and potential biases.</p>
</div>


<h2>Unit Length and Format</h2>

<p><b>Total Duration:</b> Approximately 3 weeks<br>
<b>Structure:</b> Twelve 45-minute lessons and one 3-day culminating project</p>

<h3>Unit Calendar</h3>

<p>Take a quick look at the lessons included in this unit using the calendar tool. This version of the calendar assumes 5 45-minute lessons per week.</p>

